M3.2 red: the authoritative intake spec run against the baseline (7b25890)

Tree:      a one-off extraction of `git archive 7b25890` into `.tmp/m3-2-red`
           (never the repository root), with `node_modules` symlinked from the
           parent checkout and this branch's `test/m3-intake.spec.ts` copied in.
           Nothing else from this branch was present — the source under test is
           the baseline's own `src/`.
Command:   cd .tmp/m3-2-red && TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp npx vitest run test/m3-intake.spec.ts
Exit:      1
Result:    15 failed | 3 passed (18)

Why this is red for the right reasons, not for a missing module: every import in
the spec resolves on the baseline (`installHeartbeatListen`, `classifyPreStep`,
`BLOCK_ADMISSION_ENFORCED`, the six tool names, the two file constants), so there
is no "cannot find module" anywhere in the transcript. The 15 failures are the
five product claims failing one by one:

- admission is still inert (`BLOCK_ADMISSION_ENFORCED` false, and the rule and
  the switch disagree);
- the six tools still answer a session with no mode record instead of refusing;
- `legacyGate` still defaults on, so the default chain is not the narrow
  listener alone, a stopped beat is not rejected by it, a continued beat is
  never charged, a user message is rewritten by the gate, a malformed batch is
  rejected by the gate, and neither the end-to-end stop nor the listen-file line
  exists;
- the observing shape still writes `observed` where the owning shape writes
  `continued`, and the intake-off load writes no listen line at all;
- registration is still the pre-M3.2 matrix (on adds two listeners, the gate is
  not an addition at all), and the gate's classifier still routes a heartbeat as
  `loop-continuation`.

The three that pass are the three that do not depend on the flip: "yes for an
enabled record" (true either way while the switch is off), the static six-name
coverage check, and "the same six calls get past admission" (which passes
trivially when nothing is enforced).

The transcript below is the command's stdout+stderr verbatim.

